*.png

# Backup files 
*.backup
*.backup_old
*_backup
data/*verify_backup*

*_backup.json
*_backup_old.json

_export_out/
data/solar-system/

# Patch-script backups. Nine were tracked until 2026-08-29,
# including a superseded master plan and a superseded skill. A
# session grepping for a value can hit one and read it as current.
# Widened 2026-08-31 (L-271): *.bak matches only names ENDING in
# .bak, so .bak1, .bak2 and .bak_L271 slipped through the sweep above
# and kept getting committed. All three shapes now.
*.bak
*.bak[0-9]
*.bak_*

# Local-only reference papers, never pushed (2026-09-10). This repo is
# public, and a journal's PDF may not be reposted even when the article
# is free to read. Keep papers in papers/ beside documentation/; git
# leaves the folder and everything in it out of every commit. A session
# that needs a paper gets it uploaded into its chat.
/papers/

# L-431 build 3 (2026-10-14): the Horizons check's verdict for the run it
# was written on. It changes on every maintenance run and is read only by
# check_horizons_confirmations.py on the same machine, the same day; the
# confirmations it rests on are tracked in data/horizons_confirmations.json.
data/horizons_check_last_run.json

# L-448 (2026-10-15): test_orbit_cache.py wrote its fixture here on every
# maintenance run, and test_output/test_orbit_paths.json was tracked, so a
# run could leave it deleted or rewritten for a commit to pick up. The test
# now writes into a temporary folder it removes; this keeps any copy left
# by an older run out of every commit.
test_output/
